course: dictionary
lesson: 3099
title: Egyptian: one word, three jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Egyptian can be a describing word, a person word, or a word about the past. Its meaning depends on the words around it. Look at «the Egyptian army». Here Egyptian describes the army, so it means from or to do with Egypt.
explain: Now look at «An Egyptian Queen thinks Suleiman must be dead.» Here Egyptian is a kind of person: a person from Egypt. Ask yourself: is the word describing something, or naming a person? That question solves most puzzles with this word.
explain: Sometimes Egyptian is about the far past. «Egyptian hieroglyphs» and «the ancient Egyptians» both point to ancient Egypt, a long time ago, with pharaohs, pyramids and mummies. Check the clues: is the text talking about today, or about long ago?
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning in the sentence and read it again. «Egyptian doctors set broken bones» still makes sense when you think of doctors from Egypt, or doctors of ancient Egypt, so read the rest of the text to find out which one.
fact: Egypt is a country in north-east Africa.
fact: «Egyptian» can be an adjective: «Egyptian pyramids» are pyramids from or to do with Egypt.
fact: «An Egyptian» is a noun: a person from Egypt. Two or more people are «Egyptians».
fact: Hieroglyphs are picture-signs. «Egyptians also wrote with hieroglyphs, which nobody could read for over a thousand years until the Rosetta Stone gave the key.»
fact: In history lessons, «ancient Egyptians» means the people who lived in Egypt long ago, with their pharaohs, pyramids and mummies.
exercise: «The Egyptian army marched across the desert.» What does Egyptian describe here? | A sort of desert plant | A kind of cloth | *The army, which is from or to do with Egypt | The sand
exercise: «An Egyptian Queen thinks Suleiman must be dead.» What is an Egyptian in this sentence? | A desert animal | *A person from Egypt | A type of writing | A kind of pyramid
exercise: «Egyptian picture-signs» were used in the first alphabet. What were the picture-signs? | Pharaohs' crowns | Mummies | *Egyptian writing signs | Pyramids
test: Sara says Egyptian is always a noun. Which sentence proves her wrong? | *«The Egyptian pyramids were built long ago.» | «Egyptian hieroglyphs are beautiful.» | «An Egyptian visited the museum.» | «Egyptians built the pyramids.»
test: In «Egyptians also wrote with hieroglyphs», what is Egyptians? | An adjective describing hieroglyphs | A place name | A verb | *A noun for people from Egypt
exam: Which sentence uses Egyptian to mean a person? | Egyptian hieroglyphs are beautiful. | *Ali met two Egyptians at the market. | The Egyptian pyramids are very old. | The Egyptian army was large.
